From: Pixelado Dev <350114043+pixeladodev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Gengis separable: built in by default; without it, loaded as a plugin from the BIOS folder

Gengis (BananaDS's 3D renderer; its README says it reproduces DraStic's 3D bit for bit) can be left out of the build
(BANANADS_GENGIS off; the core's build: PIXELADO_CORE_GENGIS=0). Such a build looks for bananads-gengis-<PIXELADO_CORE_ABI>.so in
the BIOS folder (render.gengis_plugin: another path), checks its interface version and that it was built against this
very tree, and uses its renderer as the 3D of melonDS's or the Banana 2D engine's renderer, with the render.gengis_*
settings and the menu's 3D effects passed through. Without one: melonDS's software 3D. The few symbols the plugin
takes from the emulator are exported (src/gengis-plugin.dynlist).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/bananads/CMakeLists.txt b/bananads/CMakeLists.txt
index 25d7a94..f705b35 100644
--- a/bananads/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/bananads/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -249,6 +249,13 @@ if(BANANADS_GENGIS)
     target_sources(bananads PRIVATE src/gengis_renderer.cpp)
     target_link_libraries(bananads PRIVATE gengis)
     target_compile_definitions(bananads PRIVATE BANANADS_GENGIS=1)
+else()
+    # Pixelado: Gengis as a plugin (src/gengis_plugin.h). PIXELADO_CORE_ABI names the tree the plugin must be built against;
+    # the symbols it takes from the emulator are exported (gengis-plugin.dynlist), nothing else
+    set(PIXELADO_CORE_ABI "none" CACHE STRING "the tree's hash, for the Gengis plugin")
+    target_sources(bananads PRIVATE src/gengis_plugin.cpp)
+    target_compile_definitions(bananads PRIVATE PIXELADO_CORE_ABI="${PIXELADO_CORE_ABI}")
+    target_link_options(bananads PRIVATE "-Wl,--dynamic-list=${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/gengis-plugin.dynlist")
 endif()
 target_compile_definitions(bananads PRIVATE BANANADS_VERSION="${PROJECT_VERSION}")
 
